.TH FPACSHELL 1 "23 September 2011" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME 
fpacshell \- command line shell for FPAC node.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fpacshell
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B fpacshell
runs a shell with MD5 protection from the FPAC node, when the Sysop
section of fpac.conf defines a command such as
.B "SYSop = /usr/local/sbin/fpacshell".
.SH WARNING
The shell is
.B /bin/sh
with the rights of
.BR fpacnode ,
which usually runs as root: whoever passes the password gets a shell on
the whole Linux system, over the radio. The password may even be typed
in plain text. For this reason the default
.B fpac.conf
leaves this line commented out; the built-in
.B SYSop
command of
.B fpacnode
only gives the sysop rights inside the node.
.P
fpacshell also opens the old BSD pseudo-terminals
.RI ( /dev/ptyXX ),
which current kernels no longer provide (CONFIG_LEGACY_PTYS), so it
stops with "Out of pty".
.SH AUTHOR
Bernard Pidoux F6BVP <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>
